/**
 * Clowder AI supplement to the generic replica runtime.
 *
 * The generic runtime (replica.js) handles declarative clickNav rules,
 * captured overlays, tabs-with-states and sidebars. Clowder additionally needs
 * behaviors the generic engine cannot express declaratively:
 *
 *  1. The 主导航 rail buttons are 40px <button>s carrying data-guide-id.
 *     verify-nav.mjs clicks clickNav targets at x=200 - outside a 40px button
 *     - so declarative rules would report constant false failures. They route
 *     by attribute here instead.
 *  2. The chat sidebar's conversation rows are <div>s with data-thread-id;
 *     clicking one opens /thread/<id>. One seeded thread capture stands in
 *     for every conversation, so they all land on thread.html.
 *  3. The settings section's sub-navigation items are query-param views of
 *     /settings; each maps to its own captured page (members is the default).
 *  4. The CLI Output fold inside a message card is an inline expand, not a
 *     portal, so capture-states cannot record it. The expanded panel body is
 *     captured verbatim below and replayed on click.
 *  5. The 审计 & Session tab row and the Mission Hub 功能列表/依赖全景 tab row
 *     swap in-page panels rather than portalling to <body>, so their inactive
 *     panels never exist in the captured DOM. The captured panel bodies are
 *     replayed verbatim; the active tab's styling comes from the source CSS
 *     classes copied from the running app.
 *  6. The chat sidebar's 自动分类 / 手动批量分类 / 猫猫训练营 buttons open
 *     modal dialogs rendered inside the app shell, not <body> portals, so
 *     capture-states cannot record them. The captured modal bodies are
 *     replayed verbatim and closed by the backdrop or the close buttons.
 *
 * The generic runtime's capture-phase listener runs first; these run in the
 * bubble phase, so navigation still wins.
 */
